esents the left antifermion endpoint of an ordered Dirac chain."}], "Usage"],
  Cell["Details", "NotesSection"], Cell["The endpoint uses an all-incoming \
external-leg label and its external mass.", "Notes"],
  Cell["The normal Dirac tag is \"Dirac\". Chiral fields use their model \
tags, rather than an assumed helicity label for a massive particle.",
   "Notes"], Cell["HEPCAT conversion uses bar v = (<p|,-[p|). This convention \
fixes relative signs in the Weyl blocks.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection"],
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Load HEPCAT", "ExampleSubsection"],
     Cell["Evaluate this setup once before the examples. The paths refer to \
